{
  "name": "Ejentic AI - Telegram RAG Orchestration",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "telegram-webhook",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "e1f13b2c-1a2b-4c3d-9e4f-5a6b7c8d9e0f",
      "name": "Telegram Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [ 250, 400 ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://backend:8002/api/rag",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-API-Key",
              "value": "={{$env.RAG_KEY_GUEST}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"query\": \"{{$json.body.message.text}}\",\n  \"clearance_level\": \"\",\n  \"platform\": \"n8n_Telegram\"\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a3b35d4e-3c4d-6e5f-1a6b-7c8d9e0f1a2b",
      "name": "Ejentic FastAPI Brain",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [ 600, 400 ],
      "notes": "SETUP: this call now needs an API key. The backend reads the caller's clearance FROM THE KEY — a body field alone no longer grants anything, so without a key this node gets 401.\n\nSet RAG_KEY_GUEST in n8n's environment (the same value as backend/.env), or replace the $env expression with an n8n Header Auth credential, which keeps the key out of the exported workflow JSON.\n\nA public Telegram bot should carry the GUEST key: anyone who can message the bot inherits whatever that key grants. Never put the executive key here.\n\nclearance_level is deliberately \"\" — it means 'everything my key grants'. It can only ever NARROW (403 if it asks for more), so it is not where access is decided."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "={{$node[\"Telegram Webhook\"].json[\"body\"][\"message\"][\"chat\"][\"id\"]}}",
        "text": "={{$json[\"response\"]}}",
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "id": "b4c46e5f-4d5e-7f6a-2b7c-8d9e0f1a2b3c",
      "name": "Reply to Telegram",
